{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur","id":1556211,"title":"The first owners of Chur","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-05T17:52:17-08:00","id":1556211,"title":"The first owners of Chur","content":"In <i>Tome of the Pentacle</i>, it Chur once belonged to the Masters of the Invoked Veil, who held the Seventh Dragon prisoner.<br /> <br /> Who <i>were</i> these beings? Mages? Other supernaturals? How long had they held Chur prior to the Tremere killing (or banishing?) them all? Could some still survive, a shattered remnant of something once both awe-inspiring yet terrifying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T18:41:56-08:00","id":1556212,"title":"","content":"They were Master mages, which is why it says &quot;warrior-Masters&quot; \u2014 <i>Left-Hand Path</i>, where the Tremere's expanded backstory was first written, specifies that there were five Masters of the Subtle Arcana who imprisoned one of the Bound in their fortress, with two stories told in parallel of the five surviving slaves of the Theban devouring the Masters of the Invoked Veil and of the five Masters defeating the breath-eating pseudovampires but being infected with their undeath.<br /> <br /> Considering this has resonance with how the Tremere create new Houses, it seems unlikely that any still exist, especially since the Invoked Veil were not mentioned to be liches and it would be quite strange for, say, a Temporal Pocket to persist in the Tremere's newly-claimed stronghold for centuries without any of them noticing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T18:47:20-08:00","id":1556213,"title":"","content":"According to page 126 of <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i>, the <i>Invoked Veil</i> were a warrior cabal known only in name. Chur is a ruin of the Time Before, resonant with the Seventh Watchtower. It is located somewhere in the Carpathian Mountains, but unknown force erased the memory and material evidence of its location in the 17th<br /> century, after the Tremere used it to defeat the<br /> Keepers of Vedet (which became House Vedmak). Not even the Tremere know it's current location or history, just that it's in that general area.<br /> <br /> So one possibility is that they were Seers keeping the Seventh Dragon in check, making it a Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T09:46:07-08:00","id":1556241,"title":"","content":"And what would that make the Seventh Dragon? A Supernal Entity? Something Abyssal? A horror from the Lower Depths? A particularly alien Insatiable? <br /> <br /> etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T10:18:17-08:00","id":1556244,"title":"","content":"The Lower Depths are places where reality is missing elements, and those Depths hunger for what they do not have. Humans cannot survive easily in the Lower Depths, so I imagine it is the embodiment of it's lack of humanity, of the human spirit. The Tremere are exposed to it, but manage to resist being fully consumed by it (which creates pretas), but the Watchtower hungers, and continues to try to consume them even as it grants them more power. <br /> <br /> A good paralel is Darth Nihilous from <i>KOTOR 2</i>, the more he feeds the hunger, the stronger he gets, but the hungrier he gets and the more he is consumed by the need to feed.<br /> <br /> Well, at least that is my theory on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T10:21:08-08:00","id":1556245,"title":"","content":"So...in your eyes, the Seventh Dragon is a fiend? Interesting.<br /> <br /> So, would that make Chur a Lower Depths <i>Verge</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T10:53:56-08:00","id":1556249,"title":"","content":"Since it's a ruin of the Time Before, in my mind Chur was a prison the Visus Draconis (aka the ancestors the Guardians of the Veil) used to contain it, the Invoked Veil were it's jailers (explaining the Veil part of the name) and the Tremere stumbled upon it in their quest for magical might. The Tremere ended up freeing it and being corrupted by it.<br /> <br /> The vanishing of Chur is some archmage shenanigans, to what end I am unsure (maybe waiting for someone to renew the seal ?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-06T12:13:31-08:00","id":1556260,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, or simply trying to banish the whole structure intobaj appropriately themed Lower Depth? It would explain thevstrangely 'non-Astral' astral sojourn a modern mage must undergo to become a proper Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T09:51:58-08:00","id":1556395,"title":"","content":"Can Tremere become archmasters? Can Tremere Ascend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:08:27-08:00","id":1556409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur?p=1556395#post1556395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Tremere become archmasters? Can Tremere Ascend?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per their core beliefs, archmasters are still running with the damage done by their having had Paths, and the only legitimate path to Ascension is through giving up your soul to the Seventh Dragon and following the Order's pursuits. The nature of both processes makes it difficult to offer conclusive answers, but the Threshold Seeking is discernible enough to other archmasters that it's not hard to suppose that a Tremere would face at least the same degree of opposite as a disloyal would-be Tetrarch,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:27:11-08:00","id":1556412,"title":"","content":"So, it's virtually impossible? What <i>would</i> a Tremere archmage be like, anyways?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:48:35-08:00","id":1556414,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">As far as I can tell, there is no official answer, so I will speculate by reading between the lines. Looking at their details in <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i>, they cannot become Rapt, beings whose unbound Supernal power burns it's way through their Gnosis into reality. Their Nimbus is faint and cannot produce a tilt. They have no Watchtower they are specifically bound to either. I think they don't have enough of a connection to the Paths to create a road accross the Abyss and into the Supernal, at least not in the traditional way. So perhaps they use another method.<br /> <br /> As to what they would be like, I theorize their Quintessences would be all about consumption. Eating souls, supernaturals, Verges, etc. They consume the Quintessence to absorb it's symbolic power and then shape it into a spell.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T14:51:36-08:00","id":1556415,"title":"","content":"If the Seventh Dragon is a Bound, what Supernal Realm would it be from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T17:01:06-08:00","id":1556419,"title":"","content":"So if we go by the Tremere's beliefs, it is difficult to map. The Seventh Dragon is resonant with souls, blood and hunger. But all the components of a soul do not map neatly to any Arcana pair. So it could be like the serpent constellation, it doesn't have a Realm and moves through the heavens in a constant hunt. After being pulled to the Fallen World, it lost it's symbols in the Supernal, explaining why the Tremere don't keep Path yantras.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could build on the samsara symbolism and make it's Realm be <b>Pretaloka</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b><br /> <b>Death:</b> The ability to hunt the soul, the common Arcana in many of their Houses, the power to eat.<br /> <b>Life: </b>The ability to draw nourishment from what Death consumes.<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum:</b><br /> <b>Prime: </b>The endless hunger for existence, why even today it constantly tries to consume Gnosis and those unable to keep it at bay become preta.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T10:04:25-08:00","id":1556429,"title":"","content":"What Supernal Entities would inhabit Pretaloka?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-10T13:13:04-08:00","id":1556438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur?p=1556429#post1556429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Supernal Entities would inhabit Pretaloka?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;He who would accomplish little need sacrifice little; he who would achieve much must sacrifice much. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/frtm4_JC_b4?si=DNETzu8FjFVazqQB\" target=\"_blank\">He who would attain highly must sacrifice greatly</a>.&quot; </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>-James Allen</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Yaoiguai are the manifest beings of Life, yokai who embody the urge to strive and slay, who forge ambition and temper it in in the fires of will.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gu</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u01d0 are the the recondite beings of Death, powerful ghosts that embody the sacrifice needed to achieve greatness, guiding those that summon them so that their sacrifices carve them into someone who can achieve their ambitions.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T05:49:25-08:00","id":1556469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur?p=1556419#post1556419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if we go by the Tremere's beliefs, it is difficult to map. The Seventh Dragon is resonant with souls, blood and hunger. But all the components of a soul do not map neatly to any Arcana pair. So it could be like the serpent constellation, it doesn't have a Realm and moves through the heavens in a constant hunt. After being pulled to the Fallen World, it lost it's symbols in the Supernal, explaining why the Tremere don't keep Path yantras.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could build on the samsara symbolism and make it's Realm be <b>Pretaloka</b>:<br /> <br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b><br /> <b>Death:</b> The ability to hunt the soul, the common Arcana in many of their Houses, the power to eat.<br /> <b>Life: </b>The ability to draw nourishment from what Death consumes.<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum:</b><br /> <b>Prime: </b>The endless hunger for existence, why even today it constantly tries to consume Gnosis and those unable to keep it at bay become preta.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Death/Life pair sounds similar to what I imagine the Sixth Dragon's pair as a theoretical Watchtower would be... of course it never managed to act completely as one the way the Seventh has, but it still makes me wonder what they difference would be if it had. Death/Life fits both the vampiric aspects of being undead and feeding on life but also fits the association the Dragon of Blood has with passing down abilities through bloodlines of other monsters as well (Life covers the physical aspects and Death the soul-shaping ones).<br /> <br /> Inferior Prime makes sense for both too... but perhaps the Dragon of Blood nigh completely lost its Supernal connections, being bound to the Lower Depths/Fallen, while the Dragon of Soul kept some, bound to the Lower Depths/Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-11T09:12:41-08:00","id":1556474,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time putting any validity in the beliefs of literal soul-eating psychopaths. It's probably a Bound that was eaten and shat back out by the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T07:34:15-08:00","id":1556557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur?p=1556474#post1556474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time putting any validity in the beliefs of literal soul-eating psychopaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere can be ruthless and cultivate a certain amorality within themselves, but I feel as though we've gotten enough books right now that lend depth and nuance to their beliefs and practices that would make them more engaging characters than a line like this might convey. Even the notion of &quot;soul eating&quot; needs to be put into context, since not only is it perfectly within their power to replace the souls that they take with their spent ones (with no indication that possession of such a thing does long term harm to the human who receives it), but they have certain incentives to do so by way of not giving away their presence by leaving behind a trail of people without souls and general sustainability. One could even have some Tremere who interpret their creed in terms of encouraging a kind of fair exchange in souls.<br /> <br /> As far as the Seventh Dragon, I feel as though that gets complicated by a question of whether the Tremere philosophy should be presented as completely delusional, or no less well-reasoned and researched than the beliefs of any given sect. I think that's supposed to be a recurring element to the horror features of Mage antagonists; the potential that they might be correct about some of what they espouse, or at least have a credible basis to believe that they do.<br /> <br /> Even if the Seventh Dragon is not Supernal directly, if it is a most profound expression of something that the Tremere believe, with cause, to be the core truth of the Supernal, then they might have basis to regard it as something that deeply resonates with the Supernal regardless of where it comes from, which might have greater implications for their model of the cosmology. After all, the Second Edition core presents such questions in terms of &quot;reality seems to incorporate some influences from alien universes, and mages can't discount the possibility that such things manage to rise up to become part of the Supernal&quot;.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, the question of &quot;what Realm does it come from&quot; might be obviated by the fact that distinct Supernal Realms are largely an illusion for the benefit of Awakening mages anyway, and there's some understanding that the Supernal beyond the influence of the Watchtowers (which itself is not fixed) is more undifferentiated. Such a thing would match with the Tremere belief that the Paths are traps and impositions.<br /> <br /> Indeed, considering what they believe the other six Dragons to be, the answer could well be &quot;apparently another Watchtower&quot;. Is it a Watchtower that has been somehow forced out of the Supernal? That raises the question of exactly where it is supposed to be right now. The question of &quot;if it is a Watchtower, who made it&quot; is mysterious in the way that the question of who made <i>any</i> of the Watchtowers is mysterious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T11:59:59-08:00","id":1556563,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The pre-Chur Tremere were operating under a philosophy of &quot;someone needs to be bold enough to make the spiritual sacrifices needed to push humanity's magical power and enlightenment&quot;. As ambitious as the Silver Ladder, following what could be seen as an offensive version of the Guardian's tenet of &quot;Sins for a just end grant Wisdom&quot;.<br /> <br /> The current Tremere are closer to the Sith. They do not stifle individual ambitions, they exalt them (so long as they don't conflict with those of other Tremere). If the truth is that magic hungers for souls, then they shall embrace it to throw off another insidious shackle of the Lie. Succeed and survive, or fail and become an empty husk.<br /> <br /> Well, at least that is how I imagine they justify their philosophy to themselves. As was mentioned above, whether they are correct or corrupted is left deliberately nebulous.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T12:03:07-08:00","id":1556564,"title":"","content":"I figure, like another poster said, some archmaster used an Imperial spell to &quot;vanish&quot; Chur. Maybe the Exarchs protected the Tremere, or an Annunaki, and Chur was all the archmaster was able to erase!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T13:57:10-08:00","id":1556567,"title":"","content":"I took the implication to be that Chur vanishing was linked to their victory over the Keepers of Vedet (actually, the timing is a bit off, though the timeline is a little ambiguous). Like, <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> says they 'used' Chur which makes me think they activated some latent ability of the fortress beyond simply using it as a defensive position.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the Tremere are kinda notable for having secret inner organisations, which makes me wonder if perhaps there's an even more secretive inner order operating out of the now hidden Chur. That'd explain why no one's found it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreatorFounderMaker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur?p=1556564#post1556564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Exarchs protected the Tremere, or an Annunaki, and Chur was all the archmaster was able to erase!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. Maybe not having access to Chur limits them in some important way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T14:29:28-08:00","id":1556571,"title":"","content":"They might've had direct leadership from the Seventh Dragon? Maybe the archmage erased Chur as a way to cut Tremere out from easy access to the Bound the Tremere thought of as a god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T15:42:36-08:00","id":1556573,"title":"","content":"Maybe the way the Keepers of Vedet were defeated was used as a Quintessence. The corrupted Chur was symbolic to consuming, and some cannibalistic cultures believed consuming someone gave you their power, so they used the Practice of Entities to make Chur take on the power of the Keepers and bind the Seventh Dragon. It's very power turned against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-13T16:38:36-08:00","id":1556578,"title":"","content":"But when a new Tremere is made Hollow, they go on a weird 'not-astral' astral trip to sacrifice a worthy soul----preferably an Awakened soul----to the Seventh Dragon. Would this mean the Tremere know where IT is, even if they can't find Chur?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-14T17:00:28-08:00","id":1556630,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Another possible direction for it is to build on the symbolism of the qlippoth of Gamchicoth, &quot;The Devourer&quot;. So maybe there existed an archmage called Astaroth (a name normally associated with that qlippoth), an Alienated who wanted to modify and Ascend Ammut, to transform it from cosmic horror into a symbol like &quot;the devourer of tyrants&quot;, into the dragon of a Path designed to combat beings like the Exarchs. He was taken out before he could pull it off, Chur was his Wending, which has an incomplete and possibly malfunctioning Watchtower prototype. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T05:41:17-08:00","id":1556640,"title":"","content":"I <i>like</i> this idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28921-creatorfoundermaker","name":"CreatorFounderMaker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T13:38:37-08:00","id":1556662,"title":"","content":"Seeing as we don't know much about Chur beyond it's name. Does anyone have any ideas as to where that name comes from?<br /> <br /> I thought it was meant as a reference back to the original Tremere chantry... But that's Ceoris (or Coeris).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-15T13:53:39-08:00","id":1556663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556211-the-first-owners-of-chur?p=1556662#post1556662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing as we don't know much about Chur beyond it's name. Does anyone have any ideas as to where that name comes from?<br /> <br /> I thought it was meant as a reference back to the original Tremere chantry... But that's Ceoris (or Coeris).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chur_(pseudo-deity)\" target=\"_blank\">Slavic pseudo-deity equivalent to the Roman god of boundaries Terminus</a> seems apropos for a location in the Carpathians important to the self-styled inheritors of the &quot;shakers of the borders.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}